Use the inclusive final byte offset when checking a reliable reset prefix.

Applies to picoquic 55b473e207e436d06ea9a2895cc1fc555d42c81c, after 0001
and 0002.
reliable_size is a byte count; picoquic_check_sack_list takes an inclusive
maximum. The formatter and ready-stream scheduler otherwise wait for an
extra byte that a header-only reliable reset never sends. The active-stream
predicate must use the same boundary and reject reactivation after a plain
reset (whose reliable prefix is empty).

This is a narrow adaptation of the prefix-boundary rule in upstream commit
8c79ccfdfe4de0e8a0f18504f9f533a5398a8103 (Christian Huitema), not a backport
of that commit's newer reset/retransmission architecture.

Tests: adapters/picoquic/tests/test_pq_reset_after_fin.c (CTest
pq_reset_after_fin). Packet rows send a reliable reset whose prefix is the
whole stream, with no FIN, both from a queued and from an acknowledged
preamble; constructed rows check the missing-last-byte, exact-prefix and
empty-prefix boundaries of the scheduler, the formatter and stream
activation.

diff --git a/picoquic/frames.c b/picoquic/frames.c
--- a/picoquic/frames.c
